   "slot": "deep-cut",
   "local": "Fjaka",
   "phonetic": "FYAH-kah",
   "context": "The Dalmatian art of doing nothing: a drowsy, contented state on a hot afternoon. Locals will tell you it can’t be translated, and then try.",
   "deepCutOrder": 1,
   "id": "dubrovnik-deep-cut-1"
  },
  {
   "slot": "deep-cut",
   "local": "Libertas",
   "phonetic": "LEE-ber-tahs",
   "context": "“Liberty” in Latin, the motto of the old republic. It was written on its flag, and you’ll see it on everything from the Summer Festival to the fort above the sea.",
   "deepCutOrder": 2,
   "id": "dubrovnik-deep-cut-2"
  },
  {
   "slot": "deep-cut",
   "local": "Đir",
   "phonetic": "jeer",
   "context": "A stroll, from the Italian “giro.” Going “na đir” up and down the Stradun in the evening is how the city sees and is seen.",
   "deepCutOrder": 3,
   "id": "dubrovnik-deep-cut-3"
  },
  {
   "slot": "deep-cut",
   "local": "Festa",
   "phonetic": "FES-tah",
   "context": "The Feast of St. Blaise, the city’s patron, on February 3. Held for over 1,000 years, with processions, flags, and the saint’s relics carried through town.",
   "deepCutOrder": 4,
   "id": "dubrovnik-deep-cut-4"
  },
  {
   "slot": "deep-cut",
   "local": "Pomalo",
   "phonetic": "POH-mah-loh",
   "context": "“Easy, slowly.” The coast’s answer to most problems, and to most requests to hurry.",
   "deepCutOrder": 5,
   "id": "dubrovnik-deep-cut-5"
  },
  {
   "slot": "deep-cut",
   "local": "Placa",
   "phonetic": "PLAH-tsah",
   "context": "What locals call the Stradun, the main street. Both come from Italian words: “piazza” and “strada.”",
   "deepCutOrder": 6,
   "id": "dubrovnik-deep-cut-6"
  },
  {
